Run the following commands sequentially to install Jenkins on your Ubuntu system.
***********Use code with caution****************

1. Install Java Prerequisites: Jenkins is built on Java and requires it to run. Update your system and install OpenJDK 21 (or OpenJDK 17):

sudo apt update
sudo apt install -y fontconfig openjdk-21-jre

2. Add the Official Jenkins Repository
The default Ubuntu repository packages are often outdated. Download the official Jenkins GPG signing key and add the stable repository to your package manager sources:
bash
# Create directory for the keyring
sudo mkdir -p /etc/apt/keyrings

# Download and add the signing key
sudo wget -O /etc/apt/keyrings/jenkins-keyring.asc https://pkg.jenkins.io/debian-stable/jenkins.io-2026.key

# Register the Jenkins repository
echo "deb [signed-by=/etc/apt/keyrings/jenkins-keyring.asc] https://pkg.jenkins.io/debian-stable binary/" | sudo tee /etc/apt/sources.list.d/jenkins.list > /dev/null


